{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"9f926ac8894ae6f9","type":"text","text":"**Edward Tasker**\n- innkeep\n- looks pragmatic, is soft inside\n- cares about everyone\n- usually silenced as his power is limited\n- wants to save everyone\n- advocates for care for the infected","x":-95,"y":-1560,"width":328,"height":318,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"744d5efa67a76eed","type":"text","text":"**Infection Blooms**\n- all infected in the tavern get insane\n- commotion is created when all infected get aggressive and their bodies start to deform\n- Innkeep advocates for more care, mercenary leader for the purge of all infected\n- if no action taken, mercenary leader executes the infected\n- the mercenaries will require body checks for everyone","x":1320,"y":301,"width":540,"height":413,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"4f7395fac70255fb","type":"text","text":"**Evening at the tavern**\n- meet with the innkeep, mercenaries, cleric, gamblers and others\n- mercenary lead is being troublesome\n- go to sleep, preferably in tavern, optionally in their own home","x":-226,"y":-400,"width":589,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"8d0c0c60dd1e2ab6","type":"text","text":"**Landfill**\n- two broken automatons, need repair\n- few infected can be found merged with some garbage magic vials and scrap\n- secrets:\n\t- few prosthetic limbs\n\t- hideout of an Eternal court member","x":2960,"y":-520,"width":420,"height":244,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"78bd40035b6c93e8","type":"text","text":"**Matteo**\n- gambler\n- advocates for freedom of choice\n- wants to save people by going out and scouting the city\n- does not trust anyone","x":-675,"y":-1540,"width":395,"height":214,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"f3e06b0284bab43e","type":"text","text":"Tools for the enemy factions:\n1. Withering Bloom:\n\t- spreads by body fluids (kiss, cough, injury)\n\t1. Fever, headaches, static noise, whispers\n\t2. Hallucinations, erratic speech, intense whispers, wounds close with hardened material, fractal patterns under skin\n\t3. Insanity and aggression, sharp bony protrusions from skin, victims sometimes freeze, jerky puppet-like movements\n\t4. Body deformation, elongated limbs, spine bends unnaturally, fingers fuse or branch, emit a low hum, may fuse with environment\n\t5. Increased aggression, merging with living creatures and magic\n\t- everyone past first stage gets turned after some time, even if they die\n\t- the only way to prevent turning in that case is burning the body or antidote\n2. Order:\n\t- 2 hooded figures\n\t\t- will not engage in direct combat\n\t\t- poison drink/food\n\t\t- poison lonely individuals\n\t\t- shoot poisoned arrows\n\t\t- carry cure vial\n\t- cleric\n\t\t- sabotage during last stand\n\t- overseer dolls\n\t\t- used to spectate the experiment\n\t\t- melts at will or after death\n\t\t- harmless\n3. Elven elder:\n\t- ravens are gathering info\n\t- uses spells to stop party\n4. Mercenaries:\n\t- loyal to the captain\n\t- end justifies the means\n5. Raiders:\n\t- unwilling to take fight\n\t- might unite if they get weapons or cure vials\n\t- blame elves and might attack","x":4090,"y":-1617,"width":710,"height":1022},
		{"id":"9551239db42e91a3","type":"text","text":"**Return to the Tavern**\n- captain wants to keep people in their homes, make group patrol the streets and have his own people look into the cause of the barrier\n- ppl in the tavern blame elves","x":560,"y":398,"width":505,"height":220,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"604b4c49aa9d6ea0","type":"text","text":"**Tavern 'Thirsty Monk'**\n- innkeep is a former adventurer and innovator\n- storage of food, water and medicine\n- secrets: \n\t  - in the basement, there is a trap door to the elven refuge\n\t  - the wine was infected the day party arrived","x":-153,"y":-1080,"width":443,"height":312,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"181c717b17122045","type":"text","text":"**Unrest**\n- poor people, gamblers and scumbags get uneasy and decide to leave the tavern and loot shops around the square\n- mercenaries do not want to allow them to leave, unless persuaded, will wipe the protesters\n- the unrest gets slowly out of hands and small fights get started\n- people eventually split into groups and loot apartments\n- weapon shop is looted as well and scumbags get weapons if not cleared before\n- some of them get ahold of one cure vial","x":2100,"y":305,"width":532,"height":405,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"cf61f33fd827b622","type":"text","text":"Tools for the adventurers\n- mercenaries can be helpful\n- cleric is gonna help (at the start)\n- innkeeper can do something\n- weaponsmith \n- EC guy has explosives\n- automatons on the landfill\n- prosthesis on the landfill\n- pastries\n- potions from the elven shops\n- elder god in the refuge\n- friendly elves","x":4090,"y":-561,"width":710,"height":401},
		{"id":"5b85a8c71dc0da08","type":"text","text":"**Clocktower**\n- metal structure with precise and beautiful clock on the top\n- no ladder or elevator\n- secrets:\n\t- the service room on top serves as a hideout for 2 ","x":3573,"y":-860,"width":327,"height":265,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"741ec61cc02f0eb6","type":"text","text":"Elven origin\n- plague is a reference to a past plague that hit humans and elves were blamed for it\n- Dome is an elven sorcery used for defense against humans","x":2974,"y":-2240,"width":466,"height":205,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"b830cd85648a141d","type":"text","text":"Infection victims\n- citizen in the alley next to weaponsmith\n- priest in the Cathedral","x":2352,"y":-1720,"width":480,"height":205,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"54f3cc213ca751fc","type":"text","text":"Two hooded figures sightings\n- seen by the elves in the refuge\n- visited tavern the day before\n- seemingly disappearing","x":2322,"y":-2240,"width":540,"height":205,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cca465dd6d9d989d","type":"text","text":"Elven weapons\n- small notched daggers made of obsidian\n- used by elven insurgents\n- can be found in the elven refuge\n- mercenary captain knows but doesn't want to tell","x":2957,"y":-1720,"width":500,"height":205,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"b3a466c7047039a7","type":"text","text":"4 glyphs\n- disabling them will not shatter the Dome\n- needed only for the Dome building\n- catacombs, bakery, astrolab, apartments","x":2998,"y":-2560,"width":418,"height":160,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"088dbd7ee66d49f2","type":"text","text":"**Elven Refuge - 3rd floor**\n- half-flooded shrine, with stairs leading from the water to a ruined altar\n- secrets:\n\t- an ancient god that offers help - for a price\n\t- able to help in a minor way for a cost of future consequences (possibly harm coming to their relative or other survivor)\n\t- need to rise up the stairs barefoot and cut a sigil of the god into the abdomen","x":1259,"y":-2220,"width":541,"height":320,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"b4a91ceb09550391","type":"text","text":"**Elven Refuge - 2nd floor**\n- illegal underground elven shrine on a sacred place, hiding elven families\n- secrets:\n\t- elven elder knows the plot, decided to go with it to help elves 'wake up'\n\t- if not saved, will get slaughtered by infected\n","x":1259,"y":-1780,"width":541,"height":282,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"aa973c6a0d3ffaa7","type":"text","text":"**Elven Refuge - 1st floor**\n- lane of small shrines, food carts, street tailors, potions, services\n- secrets:\n\t- dwarven alchemist seen two figures, definitely not elves. wants to sell something in return first\n\t- some kid seen the fight between elder elf and the order squad","x":1259,"y":-1400,"width":541,"height":260,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"0f89c0996b49b4ea","type":"text","text":"**Magic Pastries bakery**\n- contains a glyph\n- pastries and sweets with random effects, which don't go bad\n- source of food and water","x":2970,"y":-920,"width":370,"height":193,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"7cd3cbd3b2b4c205","type":"text","text":"**Imperial Order Squad**\n- masked group hiding somewhere under the Dome\n- casted Dome and sending disease to kill off population\n- plan on framing the Elves and justifying their oppression\n- goal is to spread the disease, eliminate any leads to the Order and frame elves\n- originally 3 of them, one got killed by the elven elder","x":416,"y":-2420,"width":599,"height":263,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"8a53498841bb599d","type":"text","text":"**Teodello d'Amura**\n- cleric of the Imperial order\n- seems friendly\n- claims he's travelling to a holy place in Capital\n- he's here to make sure everything goes right\n- wants to clear the name of the Order\n- secrets:\n\t- nervous the day before\n\t- not going out of his way\n\t- defends church","x":445,"y":-1997,"width":539,"height":337,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"12cb1d5df8f34ac7","type":"text","text":"**Weapon shop**\n- victim reports he was attacked by someone in the back alley next to the weapon shop\n- secrets:\n\t- owner is Thalrik Karal, a dwarven weaponsmith, found hidden in the back\n\t- seen two caped figures attack the victim and then disappear\n\t- weaponsmith is a coward but wants to be helpful\n\t- shop is looted and owner is killed if no one helps him","x":2143,"y":-160,"width":446,"height":387,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"be01a20b67cc922d","type":"text","text":"**Apartments**\n- secrets:\n\t- roof contains a glyph\n\t- nearby is one of the two Church members who tried to betray the other one, has limited info, has a cure vial but is unable to take it himself","x":2160,"y":-1300,"width":412,"height":250,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"475cda054b580300","type":"text","text":"Hideout\n- clues that it is a Church orchestrated\n- the infected will start to converge on the living\n- the magic causes infected to become enraged\n- ritual how to shatter the Dome","x":2991,"y":-3000,"width":432,"height":206,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"dc6d9609dd0c223a","type":"text","text":"Dome shattering\n- during the time of the ritual, infected will become enraged and attack the civilians\n- ","x":3021,"y":-3400,"width":372,"height":300,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"51fcb7eb6119f022","type":"text","text":"Hooded figure unveiling\n- hooded figures might make a mistake and get caught\n- one member might try to betray the other and die\n- interrogation reveals their alignment and hideout","x":2322,"y":-2560,"width":540,"height":160,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"17fc8d4378c6895f","type":"text","text":"**Church hideout**\n- notes about disease\n- ritual to shatter the Dome\n- cure vial","x":3556,"y":-1215,"width":361,"height":175,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"d1397d03234a645b","type":"text","text":"**Absolution Square**\n- monument commemorating the integration of elves into the Imperium\n- large Imperial cathedral stands in the middle\n- multiple of shops, boutiques and restaurants\n- industrial part and religious part\n- secrets:\n\t- built on top of an ancient elven holy site\n\t- entrance to elven refuge","x":2116,"y":-786,"width":500,"height":313,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"c04ee91313405c27","type":"text","text":"**Under the Dome**\n- woken up before the dawn (no long rest?), the force field has surrounded the square\n- crowd forms on the square, mercenary handles the panic and sends everyone to their homes\n- the force field is opaque, black as a night sky with dim stars, someone claims they were  transported to another place\n- secrets:\n\t- investigation reveals abjuration school and inability to bypass the field by any means\n\t- detect magic senses ppl behind the Dome","x":-180,"y":288,"width":499,"height":440,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"0d6a58dce7ebc614","type":"text","text":"**Derelict Astrolab**\n- is way bigger on the inside than the outside\n- reception is separated from the rest by some large chasm, the bridge is long gone\n- secrets:\n\t- contains glyph on the top, one infected is merged right with it\n\t- a device for tracking starts on the top\n\t- broken telescope\n\t- the ancient records show stars disappearing","x":3573,"y":-475,"width":407,"height":415,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"0d4c8088cf6ac2bb","type":"text","text":"**Catacombs**\n- primeval tunnels adorned with thousands of handprints\n- secrets:\n\t- contain a glyph","x":720,"y":-1220,"width":350,"height":216,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"c8b73e0dac52f689","type":"text","text":"**Girthilvor The Farseeing**\n- elven elder\n- blind, with raven on the shoulder\n- knows about the Imperial plot, wants to let it succeed so young elves will go to war against the order\n- uses ravens to survey the city\n- if the party tries to stop the plot, he sends assassins against them\n- owns antidote to the infection\n- elven blades can be seen\n- killed one of the order squad at the very start\n- can cast spells with ravens as his mediator:\n\t- [Grasping Vine](https://dnd5e.wikidot.com/spell:grasping-vine) \n\t- [Ice Storm](https://dnd5e.wikidot.com/spell:ice-storm)\n\t- [Bones of the Earth](https://dnd5e.wikidot.com/spell:bones-of-the-earth)\n\t- [Flesh to Stone](https://dnd5e.wikidot.com/spell:flesh-to-stone)\n\t- [Reverse Gravity](https://dnd5e.wikidot.com/spell:reverse-gravity)","x":1259,"y":-2897,"width":541,"height":520,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"049319cc7ff94a95","type":"text","text":"**Attack on the Elves**\n- unless they are evacuated the elves get slaughtered\n- if the party gets there, they get a chance to save a few elves\n- secrets:\n\t- elven elder survives in a secret room under his 'throne'\n\t- the monsters get there through the catacombs","x":2794,"y":335,"width":405,"height":344,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a58a5fc4927018e4","type":"text","text":"**Preparations for the attack**\n- more and more people come back scared because they are getting picked off one by one\n- creatures in the dark, on the rooftops can be seen\n- slowly getting bolder\n- PCs should prepare and build traps, walls, talk to NPCs, get resources","x":3367,"y":335,"width":380,"height":344,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"77cb08004f970736","type":"text","text":"**Fall of the Dome**\n- during the final attack, the heroes cast a ritual to shatter the Dome\n- if cleric is still alive, will try to stop them\n- support from the outside comes and helps the survivors","x":3900,"y":348,"width":379,"height":319,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b06cbe24b6c2e47f","type":"text","text":"Final fight\n- each fight 5-6 rounds\n- need tavern blueprint, probably on paper\n- 2 fronts - direct fight and surroundings\n\t- direct fight - loss if squad gets downed or lets infected near civilians\n\t- surroundings - rating:\n\t\t- 10+ complete success\n\t\t- 8-9 structural damage\n\t\t- 6-7 civilians injured\n\t\t- 4-5 some civilians dead\n\t\t- 2-3 ritual at risk\n\t\t- 0-1 need to evacuate\n- after each round, determine the resources lost (narratively or by roll)\n- general checks:\n\t- mercenaries present?\n\t- mercenary captain present?\n\t- elves present?\n\t- commoners fighting?\n\t- additional weapons?\n\t- healer available?\n\t- healing remedies available?\n\t- morale high?\n- 3 rounds, total one hour:\n\t- 1st round - flanks and lurks\n\t\t- surroundings fortified?\n\t\t- mercenary captain infected?\n\t\t- traps laid?\n\t\t- fight - common infected and melted flesh through the windows, captain through the front\n\t- 2nd round - frontal assault\n\t\t- front porch fortified?\n\t\t- traps laid?\n\t\t- aoe attacks?\n\t\t- fight - siren and horde of infected through the front\n\t- 3rd round - villains rise\n\t\t- cleric alive?\n\t\t- church squad alive?\n\t\t- ec guy alive?\n\t\t- fight - church squad will launch frontal assault, bombarding the place, cleric will unleash infected in the hospital, ec guy will come if the fight moves closer to the tavern and threaten to blow it up","x":3747,"y":920,"width":691,"height":1180},
		{"id":"4bbd97ace20d5725","type":"text","text":"Independent clues\n- Dome did not transport them, just isolated them\n- Praxas was in love with an elf, wants to protect the Elves at all cost\n- weapons used are elven\n- dome is an old elven magic\n- there was a plague long time ago, it is said it was spread by elves\n- two caped ppl going around spreading infection\n- there were three, one got killed by Girthilvor\n- the square was built on an ancient non-human holy site\n- most of the tavern is infected as the beer was contaminated","x":4090,"y":-124,"width":710,"height":404},
		{"id":"43959bc3281761e0","type":"text","text":"**Praxas**\n- old Felidar, missing an eye and a leg\n- prosthetic leg\n- snorts some white powder all the time to silence the pain\n- assertive, calculating and cold\n- number one priority is stopping the disease so it does not spread further\n- gets into conflict with other survivors\n- refuses to let the Dome down until cure is found\n- advocates killing off the infected\n- adjutant - Lucius","x":-760,"y":-1125,"width":428,"height":403,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"24dd554496369f45","type":"text","text":"**Markuss**\n- gnome\n- smoking cigarette, he is a soldier of the 59th  division of the 3rd Imperial army \n- ended up here by sneaking away to meet a local woman in the tavern\n- secrets:\n\t- called Quill\n\t- Eternal court member\n\t- on his own to prevent something\n\t- has hidden explosives in case things go really bad\n\t- his org did not trust his suspicions \n\t- pyrotechnic  squad","x":2943,"y":-160,"width":455,"height":428,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"1ab6b77a38a5bf7d","type":"text","text":"**Aftermath**\n- party is revered as heroes\n- crowd gathers, everyone wants to know what happened\n- Filip will hear a voice in his head that tells him, he should blame it on the Empress\n- no matter what they say, crowd will cheer and it will have consequences","x":4445,"y":382,"width":591,"height":251,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"ba933448c96aaad7","type":"text","text":"**Imperial Cathedral**\n- beautiful portraits of the Imperial family (Teva, mum, uncle and cousins)\n- secrets:\n\t- detect magic or asking NPCs might uncover the center of the dome is in the main tower of the cathedral\n\t- in the tower there is an infected Imperial priest killed by a blade, no sign of struggle\n\t- blade is elven, cannot be identified, have to have good relation with captain\n\t- all priests are dead, killed by the elven weapon\n\t- underground room?","x":1270,"y":-829,"width":520,"height":400,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"17435849c1fd4f23","type":"text","text":"**Overseer dolls**\n- way to spectate the experiment ","x":-160,"y":-1924,"width":420,"height":192,"color":"4"}
	],
